id: 23
hanzi: 晒
pinyin: shài
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to dry in the sun; to bask; to expose to sunshine; to share/showcase online
  es: secar al sol; solear; tomar el sol; exhibir o compartir en redes sociales

senses[3]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to expose objects (clothes, quilts, crops) to sunshine for drying or sanitizing | secar o airear ropa, cereales o edredones al sol | 晒被子 (dry quilts in the sun)
  2 | Verb | Standard | to bask under the sun (for warmth or tanning) | tomar el sol; broncearse; asolearse | 晒太阳 (bask in the sun)
  3 | Verb | Colloquial | to post, showcase, or flaunt photos and lifestyle on social media | compartir fotos o presumir en redes sociales | 晒朋友圈 (post on Moments)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 趁着周末晴空万里，母亲一大早就把家里的几床厚棉被抱到楼顶晒衣绳上充分晾晒。 | Chènzhe zhōumò qíngkōng-wànlǐ, mǔqīn yí dà zǎo jiù bǎ jiālǐ de jǐ chuáng hòu miánbèi bào dào lóudǐng shàiyīshéng shàng chōngfèn liàngshài. | Taking advantage of the cloudless weekend sky, mother took several thick cotton quilts to the rooftop clothesline early to dry under the sun. | Aprovechando el cielo despejado del fin de semana, mi madre subió de buena mañana los edredones de algodón a la azotea para airearlos al sol.
  #2 | 在高原地区进行户外实地科学考察时，研究队员必须涂抹防晒霜并佩戴墨镜，以防止强烈的紫外线晒伤皮肤。 | Zài gāoyuán dìqū jìnxíng hùwài shídì kēxué kǎochá shí, yánjiū duìyuán bìxū túmǒ fángshàishuāng bìng pèidài mòjìng, yǐ fángzhǐ qiángliè de zǐwàixiàn shàishāng pífū. | When conducting field scientific research in plateau regions, researchers must apply sunscreen and wear sunglasses to prevent intense UV rays from sunburn. | Durante las expediciones científicas en zonas de meseta, los investigadores deben aplicarse protector solar y gafas oscuras para no quemarse con la radiación ultravioleta.

