  风吹日晒 | fēng chuī rì shài | weathered by wind and scorched by sun; endure outdoor hardship
  饱经风霜 | bǎo jīng fēng shuāng | weather-beaten; having experienced many hardships of life
  烈日炎炎 | liè rì yán yán | the blazing sun scorching hot

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  晒 | shài | dry in sun; bask; expose | secar al sol; solear; asolearse | 日 | sun / day | 日 (sun radiating light and warmth) | 西 (xī, west / phonetic) | 10 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound where sun radical 日 combines with phonetic 西; simplified from traditional 曬. | Hanging fresh fabrics outside as the bright sun (日) sets toward the west (西) to bake in warmth. | Extender telas al aire libre mientras el sol (日) brilla cálido hacia el poniente (西) absorbiendo la luz. | 51 | AMCW | 曬

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Letting the bright sun (日) shine down onto your belongings dries and warms (晒) them through and through.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Dejar que el sol (日) ilumine los tejidos logra secar y calentar (晒) cada fibra con su brillo.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In rural China, '晒' is the centerpiece of seasonal labor—drying harvested grain, drying autumn chilies, and airing heavy cotton quilts so they smell of 'the aroma of sunshine' (阳光的味道).
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Pronounced in the 4th tone with a sharp falling pitch: 'shài' (51). Distinguish from 4th tone homophones like 'shài' (筛 is 1st tone shāi).

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    洒 | sǎ | sprinkle; spill | Has 氵 (water) on the left instead of 日 (sun)
    栖 | qī | perch; roost | Has 木 (wood) on the left instead of 日
    西 | xī | west | Standalone phonetic component without left sun radical 日
    昭 | zhāo | bright; evident | Has 召 on the right of 日 instead of 西
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    日晒 | rì shài | sun exposure; insolation
    晾晒 | liàng shài | dry in the sun and air
    晴朗 | qíng lǎng | sunny and bright
    映照 | yìng zhào | shine upon; reflect

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 晒 requires the direct thermal energy of sunlight to heat, dry, or disinfect physical objects or human skin.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 晒 vs. 晾 | liàng | 晒 relies on direct radiant sunlight to dry and heat, whereas 晾 emphasizes hanging items in a ventilated, shaded, or breezy space to dry without requiring sun (e.g. 晾在屋檐下).
    2 | 晒 vs. 烤 | kǎo | 晒 utilizes natural solar warmth, while 烤 involves artificial fire, an oven, or an electric heater (e.g. 烤面包, 烤火).
    3 | 晒 vs. 烘 | hōng | 晒 relies on outdoor sunshine, whereas 烘 implies using hot air or a specialized mechanical tumble dryer (e.g. 烘干机).

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 阳光明媚的周末，小区的阳台上铺满了各色被褥。经过整整一个下午的暴晒，棉絮里吸饱了太阳的温暖与干爽。扑倒在刚晒好的被子里深吸一口气，那熟悉的青草香气让人彻底卸下周身疲惫。 | Yángguāng míngmèi de zhōumò, xiǎoqū de yángtái shàng pūmǎn le gèsè bèirù. Jīngguò zhěngzhěng yí gè xiàwǔ de bàoshài, miánxù lǐ xī bǎo le tàiyáng de wēnnuǎn yǔ gānshuǎng. Pūdǎo zài gāng shài hǎo de bèizi lǐ shēn xī yì kǒu qì, nà shúxī de qīngcǎoxiāng qì ràng rén chèdǐ xièxià zhōushēn píbèi. | On a bright weekend, residential balconies fill with colorful bedding. Baked throughout the afternoon, cotton absorbs the sun's warmth. Collapsing onto the sun-dried quilt with a deep breath, familiar fresh scents dissolve all exhaustion. | En fines de semana soleados, los balcones se llenan de colchas. Tras una siesta bajo el sol, el algodón absorbe calidez y pureza. Al tenderse en la colcha recién soleada aspirando su fragancia, el cuerpo se libera de toda fatiga.
  #2 | 传统中药材炮制工艺中的“日晒”绝非单纯脱水，而是借助特定波长的紫外线促进活性成分转化的关键生化环节。科研机构通过光谱模拟与控温干燥技术，成功实现了传统晒制工艺的数字化与标准化升级。 | Chuántǒng zhōngyàocái páozhì gōngyì zhōng de "rìshài" juéfēi dānchún tuōshuǐ, ér shì jièzhù tèdìng bōcháng de zǐwàixiàn cùjìn huóxìng chéngfèn zhuǎnhuà de guānjiàn shēnghuà huánjié. Kēyán jīgòu tōngguò guāngpǔ mónǐ yǔ kòngwēn gānzào jìshù, chénggōng shíxiàn le chuántǒng shàizhì gōngyì de shùzìhuà yǔ biāozhǔnhuà shēngjí. | Sun-drying in traditional medicine preparation is not mere dehydration, but a photochemical phase transforming active compounds via UV wavelengths. Research centers simulate solar spectra to standardize traditional drying methods digitally. | El soleado en la medicina tradicional supera la deshidratación; los rayos ultravioleta activan fitoquímicos esenciales. Laboratorios modernos reproducen espectros solares para industrializar este método milenario con rigor científico.
